  "notes": "Almost always appears in the past participle form しゃれた, functioning as a modifier meaning \"stylish\" or \"chic.\" The kanji form {洒落|しゃれ}る exists but is rarely used. Related to the noun {洒落|しゃれ} (wit, joke, pun), though the verb focuses on stylishness rather than humor.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- しゃれた{店|みせ}: a stylish shop\n- しゃれた{服|ふく}: fashionable clothes\n- しゃれた{雰囲気|ふんいき}: a chic atmosphere\n- しゃれた{名前|なまえ}: a clever/witty name\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- おしゃれ: stylish, fashionable — the more common everyday word for being well-dressed or trendy; derived from the same root\n- {粋|いき}: chic, refined — carries a traditional Japanese aesthetic sensibility; suggests understated elegance\n- スタイリッシュ: stylish — a loanword from English, used for modern/Western-style trendiness",
